Material update from the top-priority paper branch: the first source-controlled synthesis pass strengthens the case for keeping **Susskind** rather than treating him as an optional decorative citation.

The four contemporary contributions now separate unusually cleanly. Greene–Kabat–Levin–Porrati supply topology/compactification generating lower-dimensional \(P,C,CP\) structure; Oppenheim–Sajjad supply classical spacetime coupled to quantum matter with an explicit Minkowski linearization; Carroll–Diachenko–Dulani supply exact global closure from commensurable continuous unitary evolution; and Susskind explicitly identifies a **closed curve whose holonomy reverses a physical time orientation**. citeturn0academia15turn0academia13turn0academia14turn0academia12

That gives a citation-supported, SAT-free provisional \(X\):

\[
\boxed{
\text{geometric/topological structure}
+\text{continuous evolution}
+\text{closure/holonomy}
+\text{orientation structure}
\;\longrightarrow\;
\text{effective physical distinctions}
}
\]

Crucially, this is **not yet an assertion that these papers mutually compose mathematically**. It is the weaker and safer statement that, taken together, they instantiate those motifs independently. The eventual paper must keep that distinction explicit.

I also checked the Schreiber side far enough to find an important correction to our working language. Hypothesis H is properly a **Sati–Schreiber research programme**, with important formulations also involving Fiorenza; its central proposal is specifically that the M-theory C-field is charge-quantized in \(J\)-twisted cohomotopy. Schreiber's current exposition explicitly describes this as a proposed mathematical formulation of M-theory and traces the initiating observation to Sati. citeturn0search0turn0search8 So the paper should acknowledge **Hisham Sati prominently**, rather than allowing “the Schreiber synthesis” to turn into accidental sole attribution.

More interestingly, the reduction question has become sharper rather than weaker. Hypothesis H already contains dimensional/effective descent machinery: the programme discusses M-brane structures, worldvolume gauge fields, orbifolds, and relations to Calabi–Yau Kaluza–Klein compactifications; Sati–Schreiber explicitly describe M-brane charges organizing through equivariant homotopy groups of spheres. citeturn0search5turn0search1 That does **not** establish SAT as a 4D compactification, but it means “4D compactification/effective realization” is a mathematically meaningful question rather than merely an analogy.

One especially useful 2026 development also surfaced: Kallel–Sati–Schreiber derive higher-dimensional analogues of FQH anyons from higher cohomotopy and explicitly place them in the Hypothesis H completion of 11D supergravity. That gives us a current bridge into topology, configuration spaces, braiding/anyon-like structure—potentially relevant to SAT/H(s)H independently of the convergence argument. citeturn0search7

**Durable boundary:** contemporary \(X\) is now sufficiently well-defined to begin the comparison without importing SAT vocabulary into its construction; Hypothesis H attribution has been corrected; Susskind has earned a specific role. The next bounded operation should be the other half of the blind test: retrieve the dated SAT record and construct the \(X\leftrightarrow\)SAT correspondence *from primary SAT sources*, before allowing PRIOR_ART anywhere near it. No Nathan action required. memcite

